            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0816" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v17/pg756"/>

                <head>310. Memorandum From the President’s Military Aide (Clifton) to the
                    President’s Special Assistant for National Security Affairs (Bundy)<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d310-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-06-27">June 27,
                    1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President [<hi rendition="#italic">2 lines of source text not
                        declassified</hi>] asked that you get the following information: <list>
                        <label>a.</label>
                        <item>A resume of what we promised the King.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d310-f2"
                            /></item>
                        <label>b.</label>
                        <item>A résumé of what they promised us, especially in regard to the action
                            they were going to take on the Jewish question, and in regard to the
                            servicemen, etc.</item>
                        <label>c.</label>
                        <item>If, as they alleged, the radio transmitters we promised them were
                            unsatisfactory, why did we offer them? If they were satisfactory, what
                            is the difference of opinion that makes them take such a dim
                            view?</item>
                        <pb facs="0817" n="757" xml:id="pg757"/>
                        <label>d.</label>
                        <item>Has the aid mission that we promised already departed? If not, why
                            not?</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>As a corollary to this, the President would like a few facts on the aid and
                    assistance we are giving the UAR, compared to what we are giving to that other
                    friend. What is the financial situation, especially in regard to oil, and what
                    do they really need; what should we be giving them?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">C.V. Clifton</hi><anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d310-f3"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
